                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Romulus CI is failing because it's detecting service fails. This seems to be the one:\n\nMay 05 20:27:24.043554 romulus (-updater)[271]: xyz.openbmc_project.Software.BMC.Updater.service: Unable to locate executable '/usr/libexec/phosphor-code-mgmt/phosphor-image-updater': No such file or directory\nMay 05 20:27:24.044313 romulus (-updater)[271]: xyz.openbmc_project.Software.BMC.Updater.service: Failed at step EXEC spawning /usr/libexec/phosphor-code-mgmt/phosphor-image-updater: No such file or directory\n\nhttps://jenkins.openbmc.org/job/CI-MISC/job/run-ci-in-qemu/23032/artifact/logs/20250505202805177000_RedfishIpmiRedfishExtendedTestBasicCi/20250505202805177000_CheckForApplicationFailures/20250505202805177000_BMC_journalctl.txt"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "This seems to be related to the binaries move from @patrick@stwcx.xyz changes, but looks like he has already fixed the paths in the recipe files.\n\n@anoo@us.ibm.com Any idea why this could be failing for romulus? Does IBM has any downstream patch which gets applied before this test run?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Since this is in Romulus QEMU, it is all the upstream image.  I'm building it to see if I've messed something up with the pkg-split results."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
